Modifications made in this fork
-------------------------------

As required by AGPL-3.0 section 5(a), the changes made relative to upstream
are listed here. See the git history for exact diffs.

* Added `calc-api/` — a thin, stateless HTTP service exposing the engine's
  public functions as a JSON API. AGPL-3.0, same as the engine.

* `core/types.py`, `chart/sade_sati.py`: `SadeSatiResult` now reports Sade Sati
  proper, Small Panoti and Ashtama Shani as three separate flags
  (`is_sade_sati`, `is_small_panoti`, `is_ashtama_shani`) in addition to the
  existing `is_active` umbrella. Previously all three were collapsed into
  `is_active`, which disagreed with reference sources that report them
  separately.

* `core/types.py`, `dosha/calculator.py`: `DoshaResult` gained `convention` and
  `basis`, so doshas whose definitions are genuinely disputed state which
  reading they applied and show the computed evidence. Kaal Sarpa and Shani
  Dosha now populate both. No verdict logic changed.

* `benchmarks/accuracy.py`: added a pinned `REFERENCE_DATE` and removed every
  clock read from the comparison path. The cached fixtures freeze each reference
  API's answer to "now" at capture time, so computing "now" from the clock made
  previously-passing assertions fail months later with no code change. Also
  corrected two comparisons that compared unlike things — a natal indicator
  against a current transit, and a strict reading against an umbrella one.

* Added `calc-api/Dockerfile`, `fly.toml`, `deploy.sh` and
  `verify_deployment.sh` — container and deployment configuration for the
  service above. The image carries LICENCE and NOTICE, and the running service
  advertises its source at `GET /` to satisfy AGPL section 13.

* `calc-api/`: KP planet and sign fields are rendered as symbolic names rather
  than raw integers. The engine's KP types declare `planet`, `sign`, `sign_lord`,
  `star_lord`, `sub_lord` and `sub_sub_lord` as plain `int` (with a comment
  saying "Planet enum value"), so they carried no enum type and reached callers
  as Swiss Ephemeris ids and 1-based sign indices. Translating them in the
  wrapper restores the documented guarantee that enums are always names. An
  upstream PR typing those fields properly would be the better fix.

(Further engine modifications will be appended here as they land. Each is also
offered upstream as a pull request.)


